LIVE PROOF — static export served locally, driven with Playwright
================================================================================
Build:  pnpm --filter @sotto/client web:export   (exit 0, 9 packs copied)
Serve:  node apps/client/scripts/serve-static.mjs 8095   -> http://localhost:8095
Key:    read at run time with
          export SOTTO_BYOK_SPIKE_KEY="$(security find-generic-password -s sotto-byok-spike -w)"
        and handed to the page only as a page.fill value (phase A) or an
        addInitScript argument (phases B/C). Never written to a file, a URL,
        or a log line. 164 characters. Harness lives in the session
        scratchpad, not the repo, and scrubs its own output before writing.
Fake mic: the learner utterance "¿Qué significa la palabra cigarra?" was
        synthesized locally with macOS `say -v Paulina` + ffmpeg (48 kHz mono
        s16 plus 45 s of trailing silence) — no API call, and long enough that
        Chromium's looping fake-audio file cannot barge in on the reply.
        45 s of tail was necessary: at 2 s the loop restarted mid-turn and the
        provider correctly cancelled its own utterance (barge-in working).

