VERDICT
================================================================================
DONE. Browser-direct BYOK works end to end from the shipped static export:
key entered through the UI on iPhone-shaped WebKit, stored on the device,
and one full tutor turn — mic in, Spanish transcription, streamed reply,
spoken back at 24 kHz — with the key reaching api.openai.com and nothing
else. 13 of 13 live assertions PASS, 15 new unit tests, 10 extended, full
`pnpm check` green in isolation.

Not covered (stated, not hidden):
  - Safari installed to the Home Screen (standalone PWA) microphone capture:
    UNTESTED, and documented as such in docs/byok.md.
  - The native (expo-secure-store) storage branch: unit-tested only through
    its fallback; no iOS-simulator run in this lane.
  - The live mic turn is Chromium-only, for the fake-audio-flag reason above.
